 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? A bike fit is a professional assessment of your cycling position. A cyclist needs to be in the right spot on the bike for it feel comfortable and efficient. A quick swap can often be done, but it depends how dead. A proper fit involves lot of fine tuning, and you' need someone with the right tools to do it properly. That' another sign. A proper fit adjusts the stem and bars for your body, and can make a huge difference. A bike shop usually covers it. A quick check from friendly cyclist is free, but a proper fit involves a lot of adjustment and can take an hour or two.",
